<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>netstandard2.0;net462;net8.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
	<LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
	<PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
	<RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/codexguy/CodexMicroORM.git</RepositoryUrl>
	<RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
	<PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
	<EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
	<IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
	<SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>

	<GeneratePackageOnBuild>True</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
	<Version>1.3.1</Version>
	<!-- Pinned at the PUBLISHED 1.2.0.0: adding a target framework is not
	     an API change, and moving AssemblyVersion would force a binding
	     redirect on the net462 consumers this package still ships for. -->
	<AssemblyVersion>1.2.0.0</AssemblyVersion>
	<FileVersion>1.3.1.0</FileVersion>
	<Authors>CodeX Enterprises LLC</Authors>
	<Company>CodeX Enterprises LLC</Company>
	<Description>The database provider code to implement support for Microsoft SQL Server using the CodexMicroORM application framework.</Description>
	<Copyright>Copyright (c) 2026, All Rights Reserved</Copyright>
	<PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/codexguy/CodexMicroORM</PackageProjectUrl>
	<PackageIcon>xSkrapeIcon.jpg</PackageIcon>
	<PackageTags>ORM microORM entity-framework database object-mapping micro-ORM entity data-access dataset linq-to-sql</PackageTags>
	<PackageReleaseNotes>
1.3.1 - Fixes, no API change:
- A retrieve that returned no rows, called with a column-definition callback,
  executed its command a second time to learn the result's shape. For a
  procedure that writes, that repeated the write and discarded its result. The
  shape now comes from the reader that already ran.
- A connection scope's command-timeout override was written to the shared
  provider, so it became the default for commands in other scopes until the
  next connection opened. Each command keeps its own scope's override; the
  provider's CommandTimeout is no longer changed by opening a connection.
- The procedure parameter cache held a live view of the first command's
  parameters, which kept that command reachable for the life of the process.
  It now stores detached copies.
- A reader no longer creates an unused SqlDataAdapter per call.
- System.Security.Cryptography.Pkcs, which arrives transitively, is pinned to
  the patched release of its line (8.0.2; 9.0.22 on net10.0) to clear
  GHSA-846f-f764-76mx and GHSA-2fmv-rv2c-59x7.

1.3.0 - Adds a net10.0 target and drops net9.0 (end of support; a net9 consumer
resolves the net8.0 assets). Requires CodexMicroORM.Core 1.4.1, which fixes a
permanent ServiceScope leak - see that package's notes.

No API change. AssemblyVersion deliberately stays 1.2.0.0 so existing binding is
unaffected on the net462 target.
	</PackageReleaseNotes>
	<PackageLicenseExpression>Apache-2.0</PackageLicenseExpression>
	<PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>false</PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>
  </PropertyGroup>

	<PropertyGroup Condition="'$(Configuration)|$(Platform)'=='Debug|AnyCPU'">
		<NoWarn>1701;1702;IDE0008;IDE0058;IDE0047;IDE0060;VSSpell001</NoWarn>
	</PropertyGroup>
	<PropertyGroup Condition="'$(Configuration)|$(Platform)'=='Release|AnyCPU'">
		<NoWarn>1701;1702;IDE0008;IDE0058;IDE0047;IDE0060;VSSpell001</NoWarn>
	</PropertyGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\CodexMicroORM.Core\xSkrapeIcon.jpg">
      <Pack>True</Pack>
      <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
    </None>
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Azure.Identity" Version="1.21.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Data.SqlClient" Version="7.0.2" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- System.Security.Cryptography.Pkcs arrives through Microsoft.Data.SqlClient and Azure.Identity at versions with
       known CPU-exhaustion advisories (GHSA-846f-f764-76mx, GHSA-2fmv-rv2c-59x7). Each target is pinned to the patched
       release of the line it already resolved, so no consumer moves to a new major version. -->
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net10.0'">
    <PackageReference Include="System.Security.Cryptography.Pkcs" Version="9.0.22" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' != 'net10.0'">
    <PackageReference Include="System.Security.Cryptography.Pkcs" Version="8.0.2" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\CodexMicroORM.Core\CodexMicroORM.Core.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <Target Name="PostBuild" AfterTargets="PostBuildEvent" Condition="$([MSBuild]::IsOSPlatform('Windows')) and Exists('C:\\Source\\WizerFood\\WizerFoodWeb\\SharedBin\\')">
    <Exec Command="xcopy $(TargetDir)*.* C:\Source\WizerFood\WizerFoodWeb\SharedBin\ /y /c" />
  </Target>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\README.md">
      <Pack>True</Pack>
      <PackagePath></PackagePath>
    </None>
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
